cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the associated manuscript, please cite it as below."
title: "Pulmonary Infections and Fatal Outcomes Associated with Clozapine: A Pharmacovigilance Study Using the FDA Adverse Event Reporting System"
abstract: >-
  Retrospective pharmacovigilance study of FAERS 2022Q1–2025Q4 (44,055 clozapine primary-suspect
  reports; 1,305 pulmonary infection–related cases; 309 fatal outcomes, 23.7%). Composite
  pulmonary infection endpoint showed a positive disproportionality signal vs risperidone
  (ROR 3.58; 95% CI 2.96–4.34; IC025 0.168), attenuated with olanzapine comparator; older age
  (aOR 1.90 per 10 years) and aspiration pneumonia (aOR 2.40) were fatal-outcome predictors;
  threshold-like dose–response above ~500 mg/d was exploratory.
keywords:
  - clozapine
  - pneumonia
  - aspiration pneumonia
  - pharmacovigilance
  - FAERS
  - disproportionality analysis
  - adverse drug reaction reporting systems
  - dose-response relationship
license: "CC-BY-4.0"   # TODO: confirm the license you will publish under
